PROJECT DEVELOPMENT RULES

- Before any task, check whether it is already implemented. If complete, do not repeat it.
- Inspect only relevant files. Avoid unnecessary project-wide audits.
- Make the smallest safe change; preserve existing working functionality.
- Do not duplicate components, services, business logic or database structures.
- Never alter Auth, RLS, database schema or existing data unless explicitly requested.
- Keep the app reusable for different rental companies. Avoid company-specific hardcoding.
- Preserve the approved premium UI and mobile responsiveness unless redesign is requested.
- Prefer existing utilities and services over new dependencies.
- Keep responses concise: changes made, build result and blockers only.
- If no changes are needed, respond briefly without editing code.